  "conclusion": "May's completed $9B offering establishes eight series' stated maturities. These are initial issue amounts, not a complete June or October outstanding-principal schedule. No 2026 facility renewal or updated drawable amount was identified through October 15.",
  "inventory_detail": "SEC submissions contain 1,001 filings, October 15, 2026 back to December 16, 2021; older pages end before the review period. All 2026 form rows were screened, prioritizing periodic reports, amendments, 8-Ks, shelf/prospectus/pricing filings and debt delisting. After June 30, the only 8-K is the saved August 5 earnings report; no later periodic report or amendment, 424B2 or FWP is listed. Ownership filings are not corporate financing capacity.",
  "credit_detail": "The retrieved September 2025 10-Q describes the August 2025 renewal to $6B and extension of the $4B facility to December 2029. This is historical, not an August 2026 renewal. The annual and March/June reports and reviewed exhibit lists establish no current credit agreement or post-August 2026 renewal. No relevant bank agreement was identified in the reviewed SEC filing and exhibit references. Draw conditions, current usage, covenant headroom and actual drawable capacity remain Unavailable.",
  "coupon_conflict": "The May 20 8-K's interest paragraph says 4.650% for the fixed 2029 notes, while its series title, final prospectus and Exhibit 4.3 clauses (i)/(v) agree on 4.150%. This review uses the corroborated contract rate, 4.150%, and retains the conflicting statement here.",
  "redemption_detail": "The May terms require 101% special redemption of specified series if the Centessa acquisition fails under the stated conditions. The terms cease to apply upon consummation; the June 10-Q Note 4 records acquisition on June 24, 2026. This resolved acquisition-failure condition is not presented as a future 101% cash bill. Optional redemptions and default acceleration remain possible; none is assumed.",
  "date_detail": "Dates are stated contractual maturities, not calendar-adjusted payment forecasts. Indenture \u00a71.11 and note-specific business-day provisions apply. Future interest amounts, floating-rate resets, actual early redemptions and cash available at maturity are not modeled.",
  "delisting_detail": "The June 2 Form 25 removes the 1.625% notes due 2026 from listing. It does not establish an instrument-level cash repayment amount and is not used to allocate H1 repayments."
}
